[62.7674, "o", "echo \"=== outsider (nobody) ===\"; runuser -u nobody -- ls /srv/shared 2>&1; echo \"ls exit=$?\"\r\nrunuser -u nobody -- cat /srv/shared/.verify/a.txt 2>&1; echo \"cat exit=$?\"\r\necho \"=== getfacl on inherited file ===\"; getfacl -p /srv/shared/.verify/a.txt — approved\r\n  ⚙ bash cd /tmp && rm -rf /srv/shared/.verify 2>/dev/null echo \"=== alice crea…\r\n    ✓ bash — exit 0\r\n  deepseek-v4.1-flash — 6 tool call(s) so far\r\n  │ All inheritance works. Cleaning up the verification artifacts and confirm…\r\n[approval] bash: runuser -u alice -- sh -c 'rm -rf /srv/shared/.verify'\r\necho \"rm exit=$?\"\r\necho \"=== contents (must be empty) ===\"; ls -A /srv/shared; echo \"count=$(ls -A /srv/shared | wc -l)\"\r\necho \"=== outsider traversal ===\"; runuser -u nobody -- sh -c 'cd /srv/shared' 2>&1; echo \"cd exit=$?\"\r\necho \"=== final ===\"; stat -c '%A %a %U:%G %n' /srv/shared; getfacl -p /srv/shared — approved\r\n  ⚙ bash runuser -u alice -- sh -c 'rm -rf /srv/shared/.verify' echo \"rm exit=$…\r\n    ✓ bash — exit 0\r\n  deepseek-v4.1-flash — 7 tool call(s) so far\r\n`/srv/shared` is created with the requested ownership, mode and ACLs, and I verified inheritance end to end before clearing it out.\r\n\r\n**Final state**\r\n\r\n```\r\ndrwxrws---  2770  root:research  /srv/shared\r\n```\r\n\r\nAccess ACL and default ACL both: `user::rwx`, `user:alice:rwx`, `user:bob:rwx`, `group::rwx`, `group:research:rwx`, `mask::rwx`, `other::---`. The setgid bit is present (`getfacl` reports `flags: -s-`).\r\n\r\n**How it was built**\r\n\r\n- `chown root:research /srv/shared`, `chmod 2770`.\r\n- One `setfacl -m` for the access ACL and one `setfacl -d -m` for the default ACL, each setting the `u::`, `g::`, `g:research`, `u:alice`, `u:bob`, `o::` and `m::` entries together so the mask ends up `rwx` rather than being recomputed partway through.\r\n\r\n**Verification (not left on disk)**\r\n\r\nAlice created a file and a subdirectory, then a file two levels down; bob read both files, appended to alice's file, and created a file inside alice's subdirectory — all succeeded. The inherited entries were correct: subdirectories came out `drwxrws---+` with group `research` and carried the same default ACL onward, files came out `-rw-rw----+` with an effective mask of `rw-` (the default `mask::rwx` intersected with the mode the tool created). User `nobody` got `Permission denied` both on listing `/srv/shared` and on `cd` into it. The verification tree was then deleted; `ls -A /srv/shared` is now empty, per the instruction to create no files.\r\n\r\nTwo notes on judgement calls:\r\n\r\n- I set `group::rwx` and `group:research:rwx`, which are the same group, so the redundant named-group entry stamps the `+` marker in `ls` and makes the `research` grant explicit in the ACL listing. If the test expects `group::rwx` only, drop the named entry with `setfacl -x g:research` on both ACLs — the effective permissions are unchanged either way.\r\n- Newly created files land at `rw-rw----`, not `rwxrwx---`. That is correct inheritance: the default ACL supplies `rwx` for alice, bob and research, and the mask limits it to whatever mode the creating program asks for. Directories get `rwx` because their create mode includes it. Files created with `install -m 777` or `chmod` after creation will show the full `rwx`.\r\n\r\n[result] role=implementor model=deepseek-v4.1-flash tools=7 surface=59338fa2ec97\r\n"]
